---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: What the check of the translations finds
    accDescr: scripts/check-l10n.mjs reads the texts that the code translates, translate() and translatePlural() in js, ->t() and ->n() in templates and lib, and the texts that lib translates later, of a ConnectionCheck, an InvalidSettingException and the errors that a run keeps, with the constants that they name. It compares them with the German catalog l10n/de.json. A text that the catalog lacks, or a German text with other placeholders than its English one, fails the check with the place in the code; it needs German words. A text that no code translates, a text twice, or an l10n/de.js that differs from l10n/de.json fails as well, and node scripts/check-l10n.mjs --fix drops the text and writes l10n/de.js anew. Otherwise the check passes.

    code["The code<br>js · templates · lib"]
    texts["`The texts it translates<br>*and those that lib*<br>*translates later*`"]
    catalog["The catalog<br>l10n/de.json"]
    compare{"Each text once in the catalog,<br>with its placeholders,<br>and nothing more?"}
    missing["❌ A missing text or<br>other placeholders:<br>add the German words"]
    unused["🔧 An unused text, one twice<br>or another l10n/de.js:<br>--fix drops it and writes it"]
    passed["✅ Passes: every text<br>is in German"]

    code --> texts --> compare
    catalog --> compare
    compare -- "missing" --> missing
    compare -- "more" --> unused
    compare -- "yes" --> passed

    classDef source fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef check fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef refused fill:#c9302c1f,stroke:#c9302c,stroke-width:2px
    class code,catalog source
    class texts,compare,unused check
    class passed done
    class missing refused
